shapes each object for our service;
from the same clay he fashioned alike
vessels serving clean purposes
and those serving the opposite;
and the clay-worker decides the use of each kind.

You priests, speak to the heart of Jerusalem; comfort her.
For her humiliation is fulfilled, her sin is loosed;
for from the hand of the Lord she has received double for her sins.

When the house was being built after the captivity; a song of David.
Sing to the Lord a new song;
sing to the Lord, all the earth.

These things you did, and I kept silent;
you conceived the lawless thought that I would be like you.
I will rebuke you and set it before your face.

Our fathers in Egypt did not understand Thy wonders;
they did not remember the abundance of Thy mercy
and provoked Thee while going up in the Red Sea.

For a potter, laboriously kneading soft earth,
shapes each object for our service;
from the same clay he fashioned alike
vessels serving clean purposes
and those serving the opposite;
and the clay-worker decides the use of each kind.

He makes grass spring up for livestock
and green plants for the service of humans,
to bring bread out of the earth;

He took care that it would not fall,
knowing that it cannot help itself;
for it is an image and needs help.

Yet when praying concerning his possessions, marriage, and children,
he is not ashamed to address what has no soul;
for health he calls upon what is weak,

He turned my soul back;
He guided me upon paths of righteousness
for His name’s sake.

A voice of one crying in the wilderness:
Prepare the way of the Lord;
make straight the paths of our God.

For even if I walk in the midst of death’s shadow,
I will fear no evils, for Thou art with me;
Thy rod and Thy staff comforted me.

They will perish, but Thou wilt remain;
all will grow old like a garment.
Like a cloak Thou wilt change them, and they will be changed.

verses.display_text:
We all, like sheep, have gone astray;
each person has strayed in his own way.
And the Lord delivered him over to our sins.

And I will give the wicked in exchange for his burial,
and the rich in exchange for his death;
for he committed no iniquity,
nor was deceit found in his mouth.

from the toil of his soul,
to show him light and fashion him with understanding,
to justify the righteous one who serves many well;
and he will bear their sins.

Therefore he will inherit many,
and will divide the spoils of the mighty;
for his soul was delivered to death,
and he was numbered among the lawless.
And he bore the sins of many,
and for their sins he was delivered up.

You who thirst, go to the water;
and you who have no silver, go and buy wine and rich food,
and drink without silver or price.

